Description: Jennifer programming language interpreter
 Jennifer is a small, experimental, interpreted programming language;
 source files use the .j extension. This package installs the standard
 full-featured interpreter (/usr/bin/jennifer) and the .j module library
 under /usr/share/jennifer/modules.
 .
 The binary is a static, CGO-free build, so it depends on no libc and runs
 on OpenWRT's musl unchanged. It needs roomy storage/RAM relative to a
 busybox applet - suitable for a NAND / x86 / extroot target, not a small
 internal-flash router. See the OpenWRT README for sizing and the
 --force-architecture note for non-default aarch64 subtargets.
